<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) (Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings)",
        "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) faithfully reproduces Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py> ;
    schema:about "Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: any quantitative match to the digitised 1917 plates (no segmentation performed in v1)",
        "does_not_claim: crystallographic (calcite vs vaterite vs aragonite) control of fibre texture",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E1/E2 interface- vs diffusion-limited radial growth tables (constant vs outward-thinning lamellae)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E3 Euclidean distance-transform front from a square nucleus: asphericity decays as R^-0.97",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E4 60-centre equal-rate Voronoi mosaic: mean 5.78 neighbours, area CV 0.561",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E5 radial Keller-Rubinow/Ostwald supersaturation precipitation in 2-D (P = 1.220, 11 bands) and 3-D (7 bands)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E6 dielectric-breakdown clusters at eta = 0 (Eden) and eta = 1 (DLA, mass-radius exponent 1.63)",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 421-422: Harting's CaCO3 precipitated in albumen forms 'large rounded concretions, with a more or less distinct central nucleus, and with a surrounding structure at once radiate and concentric'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 422: crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines'; p. 426: pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 424: with scanty albumin / scanty supply the globules become rough 'by an outgrowth of spinous or digitiform projections'",
        "reported_in_source: p. 427: Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre', offered as the cause of the concentric striation",
        "transfer_boundary: 2-D sections of 3-D spherites; synthetic spherite texture is illustrative only",
        "transfer_boundary: ooids and silver-chromate rings are modern analogues, not Harting's albumen spherites" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py; output: docs/media/t1917_023_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png; organism: Harting calcospherites (CaCO3 in egg albumen); natural analogues: plaice otoliths (Fig. 209), Jurassic ooids, silver-chromate Liesegang rings; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 421-422: Harting's CaCO3 precipitated in albumen forms 'large rounded concretions, with a more or less distinct central nucleus, and with a surrounding structure at once radiate and concentric' | p. 422: crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines'; p. 426: pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles' | p. 424: with scanty albumin / scanty supply the globules become rough 'by an outgrowth of spinous or digitiform projections' | p. 427: Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre', offered as the cause of the concentric striation; reconstructed_in_script: E1/E2 interface- vs diffusion-limited radial growth tables (constant vs outward-thinning lamellae) | E3 Euclidean distance-transform front from a square nucleus: asphericity decays as R^-0.97 | E4 60-centre equal-rate Voronoi mosaic: mean 5.78 neighbours, area CV 0.561 | E5 radial Keller-Rubinow/Ostwald supersaturation precipitation in 2-D (P = 1.220, 11 bands) and 3-D (7 bands) | E6 dielectric-breakdown clusters at eta = 0 (Eden) and eta = 1 (DLA, mass-radius exponent 1.63); transfer_boundary: 2-D sections of 3-D spherites; synthetic spherite texture is illustrative only | ooids and silver-chromate rings are modern analogues, not Harting's albumen spherites; does_not_claim: any quantitative match to the digitised 1917 plates (no segmentation performed in v1) | crystallographic (calcite vs vaterite vs aragonite) control of fibre texture]; other sources: On Growth and Form (1st ed.), Ch. IX On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons, pp. 411-487 <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-023-on-concretions-spicules-and-sp-audit-thompson1917-t1917-023-8> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.65e-01 .

