<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring (L1-33) and section headers map E1-E6 to Thompson page numbers and to the Lean module; function docstrings cite Zener / Mullins-Sekerka, Keller-Rubinow/Ostwald, Niemeyer et al. Figure numbers (195-197, 208) are pinned to pixel boxes (L55-61) but the link from each measured number back to a specific Thompson sentence is not yet explicit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) — Model fidelity to source: 66/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1-E5 are implemented as stated in the reference JSON and match the Lean theorems (`radial_growth_laws` L110-121, `simulate_front_rounding` L125-153, `simulate_voronoi_impingement` L157-180, `simulate_liesegang_radial` L184-232, `simulate_dbm_cluster` L236-288). The Liesegang solver is the Ostwald supersaturation form with explicit nucleation / growth thresholds and d-dimensional radial Laplacian. However the sphericity-stability law is only exercised for uniform (isotropic) deposition; the anisotropic crystalline alternative that Thompson contrasts (calcium oxalate stays crystalline, p. 434) is not implemented, and the Mullins-Sekerka regime boundary is not swept." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py L66–L72: no anisotropic-deposition alternative and no threshold-free Liesegang control in PARAMS <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L66-L72>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
