    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) — MorphoEval overall 56.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline. The script implements the five Lean-backed geometric laws (constant lamella, parabolic thinning, asphericity decay, Voronoi impingement, geometric Liesegang spacing) and a dielectric-breakdown supply model, verifies the SHA-256 of all five vendored plates/specimens, and renders the plates beside the model panels. Simulation-side numbers are close to their analytic/literature references (asphericity exponent -0.97 vs -1, Voronoi neighbours 5.78 vs 6, Liesegang P = 1.22 inside the 1.05-1.4 Jablczynski range), but the plates and the two analogue specimens are displayed, not measured: no segmentation, no fit statistics, no negative/ablation controls, and only two points of the eta sweep. The claim is therefore not yet tested against Thompson's own figures. Overall 56.5/100 (faithfulness 50.4, reproducibility 70.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit ae9bb0083; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 66, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 48, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 80, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_023_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py at ae9bb0083, image/png, 1067896 B, 2200×1100 px, artifact_sha256 99d274958a29f4bd87f9aaff461949ff9ec5963481105a8e0847935d5196621b (sha256 99d274958a29f4bd87f9aaff461949ff9ec5963481105a8e0847935d5196621b), spec_fingerprint 09c3115074722edd88f58e645bafec8f465e6fa5a4c47f5f66ece6a0c71a3acd. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 09c3115074722edd88f58e645bafec8f465e6fa5a4c47f5f66ece6a0c71a3acd; artifact_sha256: 99d274958a29f4bd87f9aaff461949ff9ec5963481105a8e0847935d5196621b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/carmel_ooids_thin_section_specimen.jpg=3f1e500de229723d..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/liesegang_rings_silver_chromate_gelatine_specimen.jpg=2f41645ff68f6000..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/paper_citations.bib=7a05770584be0d5e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/scout_manifest.json=89dbc647da5d51c9..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/t1917_023_on_concretions_spicules_and_sp_reference.json=23dafa48d0e5c552..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/thompson_1917_p421_figs195-196_harting_calcospherites.jpg=f05b4d1f9ce006b8..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/thompson_1917_p422_fig197_aggregated_calcospherites.jpg=65eabed4733a09dd..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/thompson_1917_p432_fig208-209_spherocrystal_otoliths.jpg=cbfffad55d3f82b7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 421-422: Harting's CaCO3 precipitated in albumen forms 'large rounded concretions, with a more or less distinct central nucleus, and with a surrounding structure at once radiate and concentric' | p. 422: crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines'; p. 426: pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles' | p. 424: with scanty albumin / scanty supply the globules become rough 'by an outgrowth of spinous or digitiform projections' | p. 427: Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre', offered as the cause of the concentric striation; reconstructed_in_script: E1/E2 interface- vs diffusion-limited radial growth tables (constant vs outward-thinning lamellae) | E3 Euclidean distance-transform front from a square nucleus: asphericity decays as R^-0.97 | E4 60-centre equal-rate Voronoi mosaic: mean 5.78 neighbours, area CV 0.561 | E5 radial Keller-Rubinow/Ostwald supersaturation precipitation in 2-D (P = 1.220, 11 bands) and 3-D (7 bands) | E6 dielectric-breakdown clusters at eta = 0 (Eden) and eta = 1 (DLA, mass-radius exponent 1.63); transfer_boundary: 2-D sections of 3-D spherites; synthetic spherite texture is illustrative only | ooids and silver-chromate rings are modern analogues, not Harting's albumen spherites; does_not_claim: any quantitative match to the digitised 1917 plates (no segmentation performed in v1) | crystallographic (calcite vs vaterite vs aragonite) control of fibre texture." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add goodness-of-fit statistics (Pearson r, RMSE, two-sample KS, CV) between simulated and specimen distributions, expose CLI parameter overrides, and write datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-023/result.json with the claim verdict.",
        "remediation needed: Add negative / ablation controls: anisotropic (chessboard-metric) deposition that does not round off; threshold-free (K_ss = K_sp) precipitation that gives a continuous deposit instead of bands.",
        "remediation needed: Analyse the two analogue specimens: ellipse fit, concentric ring count and radial-fibre alignment of the Carmel ooids; ring radii of the silver-chromate Liesegang specimen with geometric-vs-arithmetic spacing fits (r, RMSE) and Jablczynski P.",
        "remediation needed: Run the full eta sweep (0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2) and the Liesegang b0 sweep (0.05, 0.1, 0.2) to show monotone control of solidity / exponent and of P.",
        "remediation needed: Segment Thompson's plates: boundary-radius CV and radial-fibre alignment of the Fig. 196 spherite, nucleus detection + radial alignment in Fig. 195, cell neighbour count / area CV of the Fig. 197 mosaic, ring radii of Fig. 208." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.65e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-023-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-023 — calcospherites grow by radial deposition about a centre (Harting 1872 artificial CaCO3 concretions in egg albumen) — Parameter expressivity: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Only two eta values (0 and 1) are run (`PARAMS['dbm']['etas']` L71), a single Liesegang (a0, b0) pair per dimension (L68-69, L297-298), and a single seed geometry for E3. The regimes listed in the reference JSON (eta = 0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2; b0 = 0.05, 0.1, 0.2) are not swept, so monotonic control of form by supply exponent and by electrolyte ratio is asserted, not demonstrated. There are no CLI overrides for model parameters." ;
