<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Interface-controlled radial deposition about a centre (constant lamella thickness, semigroup growth law)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises Thompson's 'deposited about some minute point or centre of crystallisation' (p. 437): a point-seeded front advancing by equal normal increments produces equally spaced concentric shells, and the growth law composes in time | Variables: R_n: radius of the spherite front after n deposition intervals; R_0: nucleus radius; v: normal deposition increment per interval (surface-reaction-limited)" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. IX pp. 421-422, 437; Hoffman & Lauritzen (1961); Keith & Padden (1963)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_023.lean#L32-L52>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L110-L121> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def radius_lin (R0 v n : Int) : Int :=
  R0 + v * n
def lamella_lin (R0 v n : Int) : Int :=
  radius_lin R0 v (n + 1) - radius_lin R0 v n
theorem lamella_thickness_constant (R0 v n : Int) :
    lamella_lin R0 v n = v
theorem radial_deposition_semigroup (R0 v n m : Int) :
    radius_lin (radius_lin R0 v n) v m = radius_lin R0 v (n + m)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dR/dt = v  =>  R_n = R_0 + v n;  R_{n+1} - R_n = v;  R(R(R_0, n), m) = R(R_0, n + m)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.radius_lin" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.lamella_thickness_constant" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Diffusion-limited radial deposition — lamellae thin outward" ;
    dct:description "Shows that when the supply is diffusion-limited the concentric lamellae become strictly thinner outward — the alternative kinetic regime against which the constant-lamella law (Law 1) is tested on the digitised plates | Variables: kappa = D Omega (c_inf - c_eq): diffusive supply constant; R_n: radius at the n-th equal-time deposit" ;
    dct:source "Zener (1949) J. Appl. Phys. 20:950; Frank (1950); Mullins & Sekerka (1963) J. Appl. Phys. 34:323" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_023.lean#L59-L100>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L110-L121> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def radius_sq_parabolic (R0 kappa n : Int) : Int :=
  R0 * R0 + 2 * kappa * n
theorem parabolic_shell_identity (R0 kappa n : Int) :
    radius_sq_parabolic R0 kappa (n + 1) - radius_sq_parabolic R0 kappa n = 2 * kappa
theorem lamellae_thin_outward (R1 R2 R3 c : Int)
    (h0 : 0 < R1) (h12 : R1 < R2) (h23 : R2 < R3)
    (hA : R2 * R2 - R1 * R1 = c) (hB : R3 * R3 - R2 * R2 = c) :
    R3 - R2 < R2 - R1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "R dR/dt = kappa  =>  R_n^2 = R_0^2 + 2 kappa n;  (R_{n+1} - R_n)(R_{n+1} + R_n) = 2 kappa;  R_1 < R_2 < R_3 with equal square increments  =>  R_3 - R_2 < R_2 - R_1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.radius_sq_parabolic" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.lamellae_thin_outward" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sphericity stability under uniform normal deposition" ;
    dct:description "Proves the geometric core of the claim: whatever the shape of the nucleus, equal radial deposition rounds the concretion off (A -> 0 as 1/R), so 'physical deposition alone' yields spherical forms in the interface-controlled regime | Variables: rho_max, rho_min: largest / smallest radial extent of the front; A = (rho_max - rho_min)/rho_min: relative asphericity" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. IX pp. 425-426 (rounded contours); Huygens/eikonal front propagation" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_023.lean#L106-L128>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L125-L153> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rho_max (Rmax0 v n : Int) : Int := Rmax0 + v * n
def rho_min (Rmin0 v n : Int) : Int := Rmin0 + v * n
theorem absolute_asphericity_conserved (Rmax0 Rmin0 v n : Int) :
    rho_max Rmax0 v n - rho_min Rmin0 v n = Rmax0 - Rmin0
theorem asphericity_nonincreasing (Rmax0 Rmin0 v n m : Int)
    (hseed : Rmin0 ≤ Rmax0) (hv : 0 ≤ v) (hnm : n ≤ m) :
    (Rmax0 - Rmin0) * rho_min Rmin0 v n ≤ (Rmax0 - Rmin0) * rho_min Rmin0 v m
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "rho_max(n) - rho_min(n) = R_max,0 - R_min,0  (conserved);  n <= m, 0 <= v  =>  (R_max,0 - R_min,0) rho_min(n) <= (R_max,0 - R_min,0) rho_min(m)  i.e.  A(m) <= A(n)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.rho_min" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.asphericity_nonincreasing" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Equal-rate impingement plane / Voronoi mosaic of crowded calcospherites" ;
    dct:description "Explains Thompson's observation that crowded calcospherites 'assume polyhedral, or often regularly hexagonal, outlines' (p. 422) and that pairs look like 'contiguous soap-bubbles' (p. 426): radial deposition from several centres partitions space into convex Voronoi cells with plane faces | Variables: x = (x,y,z): a point of the common boundary; c_1, c_2: nuclei of two simultaneously nucleated, equal-rate spherites" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. IX pp. 422, 426; Ch. VII (hexagonal close packing)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_023.lean#L134-L163>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L157-L180> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sqdist (x y z a b c : Int) : Int :=
  (x - a) * (x - a) + (y - b) * (y - b) + (z - c) * (z - c)
theorem impingement_locus_is_affine (x y z a1 b1 c1 a2 b2 c2 : Int) :
    sqdist x y z a1 b1 c1 - sqdist x y z a2 b2 c2 =
      2 * (a2 - a1) * x + 2 * (b2 - b1) * y + 2 * (c2 - c1) * z
        + (a1 * a1 + b1 * b1 + c1 * c1) - (a2 * a2 + b2 * b2 + c2 * c2)
theorem midpoint_on_impingement_plane (a1 b1 c1 a2 b2 c2 : Int) :
    sqdist (a1 + a2) (b1 + b2) (c1 + c2) (2 * a1) (2 * b1) (2 * c1) =
      sqdist (a1 + a2) (b1 + b2) (c1 + c2) (2 * a2) (2 * b2) (2 * c2)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "|x - c_1|^2 - |x - c_2|^2 = 2 (c_2 - c_1) . x + |c_1|^2 - |c_2|^2  (affine in x)  =>  the boundary of two equal spherites is the perpendicular-bisector plane; the midpoint (c_1 + c_2)/2 lies on it" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.sqdist" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.impingement_locus_is_affine" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-023-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Liesegang 'logarithmic ratio' band spacing (Jablczynski law)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises Thompson's quantitative statement that Liesegang zones 'stand farther and farther apart, in logarithmic ratio, as they recede from the centre' (p. 427), which he offers as the cause of the concentric striation of calcospherites; the script tests the geometric law against the silver-chromate specimen and the E5 simulation | Variables: r_n: radius of the n-th concentric band; P: Jablczynski spacing coefficient (1.05-1.4 empirically); gap_n = r_{n+1} - r_n" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) Ch. IX p. 427; Jablczynski (1923) Bull. Soc. Chim. Fr. 33:1592; Antal et al. (1998) J. Chem. Phys. 109:9479" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_023.lean#L170-L195>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ae9bb0083/thompson/claims/t1917-023_on-concretions-spicules-and-spicular-skeletons.py#L184-L232> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def band_radius (r0 P : Nat) (n : Nat) : Nat :=
  r0 * P ^ n
def band_gap (r0 P : Nat) (n : Nat) : Nat :=
  band_radius r0 P (n + 1) - band_radius r0 P n
theorem band_ratio_constant (r0 P n : Nat) :
    band_radius r0 P (n + 1) = P * band_radius r0 P n
theorem geometric_band_gap_grows (r0 P n : Nat) :
    band_gap r0 P (n + 1) = P * band_gap r0 P n
theorem band_gap_monotone (r0 P n : Nat) (hP : 1 ≤ P) :
    band_gap r0 P n ≤ band_gap r0 P (n + 1)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_n = r_0 P^n;  r_{n+1} = P r_n;  gap_{n+1} = P gap_n;  P >= 1  =>  gap_n <= gap_{n+1}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02866341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sedgeo.2016.02.008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1702607>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.477609>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.47.1400>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.1033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.s2-12.46.118> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "mechanistic-geometric — radial deposition about a centre (Thompson 1917 Ch. IX claim T1917-023)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.band_radius" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_218.geometric_band_gap_grows" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

